4 3
3 3
5 1
2 4
1 10

Snakes:
1. $T=3, L=3$
2. $T=5, L=1$
3. $T=2, L=4$
4. $T=1, L=10$

$k=1$:
1. $3 \times (3+1) = 3 \times 4 = 12$
2. $5 \times (1+1) = 5 \times 2 = 10$
3. $2 \times (4+1) = 2 \times 5 = 10$
4. $1 \times (10+1) = 1 \times 11 = 11$
Max is 12.

$k=2$:
1. $3 \times (3+2) = 3 \times 5 = 15$
2. $5 \times (1+2) = 5 \times 3 = 15$
3. $2 \times (4+2) = 2 \times 6 = 12$
4. $1 \times (10+2) = 1 \times 12 = 12$
Max is 15.

$k=3$:
1. $3 \times (3+3) = 3 \times 6 = 18$
2. $5 \times (1+3) = 5 \times 4 = 20$
3. $2 \times (4+3) = 2 \times 7 = 14$
4. $1 \times (10+3) = 1 \times 13 = 13$
Max is 20.

